      "text": "{\"unit_id\": \"Kemsit\", \"choices\": [], \"reasoning\": \"Record 1, Kemsit, renders the consonants k-m-s, a weak i, and a final t. That t is a feminine ending, so the name corresponds to something like Kmsj.t. The rules allow a record to omit a feminine t, but not to add a t the candidate lacks. C1 Kꜣ-ms.w (Ka-mesu) is the words kꜣ + ms.w, with no t; Kemsit's final t is a consonant C1 lacks, and C1 ends in plural .w, not a feminine ending, so it does not match. C2 Kms=j-w (Kemesi-u) is kms + suffix =j + w, with no t, so Kemsit adds a consonant and does not match. C3 Kwms (Kumes) is k-w-m-s with no t, so Kemsit adds a final t and does not match. C4 Kms (Kemes) is k-m-s with no t; Kemsit adds a weak i and a t, the i is acceptable as a vowel but the t is not in the candidate, so it does not match. None of the candidates carries the feminine ending, so none is the same name as Kemsit.\"}"
